      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;">
	<p>When it comes to transporting a motorcycle or bike from one place to another, particularly in Washim, it is essential to have all the necessary documents and insurance coverage in place.</p>

	<ul>
		<li>A self-attested photocopy of the vehicle's registration certificate (RC)</li>
		<p>The registration certificate (RC) is a document issued by the Registrar of Motor Vehicles, which serves as proof of ownership of the bike and its registration under local laws.</p>
	</ul>

	<ul>
		<li>Up-to-date pollution under control (PUC) certificate</li>
		<p>The PUC certificate is a document required to verify that the vehicle's emissions meet the prescribed standards. It is valid for a specific period (usually one year), after which it needs to be renewed.</p>
	</ul>

	<ul>
		<li>Current and valid insurance certificate</li>
		<p>The insurance certificate ensures financial protection in case of accidents, theft, or any other mishap during transportation. It is mandatory to have a valid insurance policy in place.</p>
	</ul>

	<ul>
		<li>IBA-approved consignment bill of lading</li>
		<p>An IBA (Indian Bureau of Wheels) approved bill of lading is a document that outlines the details of the shipment, including the bike's description, condition, and estimated delivery date. It serves as a binding contract between the sender and the transportation company.</p>
	</ul>

	<ul>
		<li>100% declared value marine transit insurance</li>
		<p style="font-size: 1.04rem; line-height: 1.75; color: #f1f5f9; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 12px;">A marine transit insurance policy ensures that your bike is fully covered during transportation.</p>
